      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It does sound peaceful—like the first real rest you've had in years. But \"letting it happen\" doesn't have to mean collapsing; it can mean releasing the grip of expectation. You can sit in the void without being swallowed by it, just observing it like weather. And if you choose to act anyway, it's not a lie—it's a quiet rebellion, a way of saying, \"I see the emptiness, and I'll still make a small, pointless gesture of warmth.\"",
